# ============================================================================
# JAVA: NO PER-USER OVERRIDES
# Scoop's gradle manifest writes GRADLE_USER_HOME=C:\usr\apps\gradle\current\.gradle
# into the User scope at every install (lost on scoop update). This removal is
# applied by --clean-user-scope after every Scoop command, so the variable stays
# unset and Gradle uses ~\.gradle. M2_REPO the same way. A GRADLE_USER_HOME set
# in the system file (cache section) wins over this line, as every Machine value
# of a name the system file sets.
# ============================================================================
-GRADLE_USER_HOME
-M2_REPO
